**1. Definitions.** “Work” means the source code, build scripts, documentation,
configuration, icons and other materials in the `patcher-lab` repository
created by the copyright holder, excluding (a) third-party components,
(b) `PclTheme.xaml` and any UI styles, fonts, icons or assets extracted from
or adapted from PCL, (c) test/build outputs and binaries under `bin/`, `obj/`
and `dist/`, and (d) “Patched Output”. Build artifacts published by the
copyright holder (such as `dist/PclPatcher.Gui.Net48.exe`) are part of the Work, but
third-party components embedded in or bundled with them remain subject to
Section 6. “Patched Output” means
any file, assembly, installer or release produced by modifying, rebuilding,
injecting into or repackaging PCL or any other third-party software using the
Work. “Personal Study and Research” means non-commercial activity by an
individual for learning, teaching, security research or technical validation,
on a software copy that the individual lawfully owns, without providing
products or services to others. “Redistribute” means providing copies of the
Work or derivatives to third parties in any form, including uploading,
publishing, mirroring, packaging, selling, renting, transmitting, bundling,
or incorporating the Work into another product.

**2. Grant.** Subject to this license, the copyright holder grants you a
worldwide, royalty-free, non-exclusive, non-transferable, revocable (as
provided in Section 7) license to (a) read and study the Work, (b) compile and
run it locally, (c) modify it locally for Personal Study and Research, and (d)
make a reasonable number of backup copies. No sublicensing is granted. No patent, trademark or trade
secret license is granted, express or implied. All rights not expressly
granted are reserved.

**3. Restrictions.** You must not: (3.1) use the Work or derivatives for any
commercial purpose, including sale, licensing, subscription, paid services,
internal business processes, or integration into commercial products or
services; (3.2) redistribute the Work or derivatives, in source or binary
form; (3.3) distribute, publish, sell or publicly provide any Patched Output,
including patched PCL; (3.4) remove, obscure or alter copyright notices,
license text, disclaimers or third-party attributions; (3.5) use the name,
author attribution or marks of the Work to imply endorsement, sponsorship or
affiliation by the copyright holder, the PCL author or any third party; or
(3.6) use the Work in violation of applicable law (including the mainland
China regulations on game publication, import and operation), PCL's
distribution license and fair-use guidelines, the Minecraft EULA, or any
third-party rights.
Section 3.6 is your independent obligation. This license grants no rights in
PCL, Minecraft or any third-party software and does not indicate that the
copyright holder endorses any particular patching, distribution or
circumvention activity.

**4. Limited Quotation.** You may briefly quote code snippets or
documentation from the Work in non-commercial commentary, teaching or
academic work, provided you attribute the source and author and do not
redistribute a substantial portion of the Work. Section 3.2 otherwise
remains in effect.

**5. No Warranty.** THE WORK IS PROVIDED “AS IS”, WITHOUT ANY EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED WARRANTY, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A
PARTICULAR PURPOSE, TITLE, NON-INFRINGEMENT, ACCURACY, OR ANY WARRANTY THAT
PATCHING WILL NOT DAMAGE FILES, CAUSE DATA LOSS OR VIOLATE LAW. YOU BEAR ALL
RISKS OF USING THE WORK. See [DISCLAIMER.md](DISCLAIMER.md).

**6. Third-Party Components.** Third-party components are governed by their
own licenses, which this license does not modify. See the table above and
[NOTICE.md](NOTICE.md). In case of conflict, the third-party license prevails
for that component.

**7. Term and Termination.** This license is effective from the date you
obtain the Work until terminated. It terminates automatically, without
notice, if you breach any term. Upon termination you must stop using the Work
and delete all copies, derivatives and Patched Output. Sections 3, 5, 6, 8
and 9 survive termination.

**8. Limitation of Liability.** TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW, THE
COPYRIGHT HOLDER IS NOT LIABLE FOR ANY DIRECT, INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL,
PUNITIVE OR CONSEQUENTIAL DAMAGES ARISING FROM THE USE OF OR INABILITY TO USE
